{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d8c5cd76-224a-4869-a534-d8e30883c446","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with a block on a frictionless incline. The slope makes an angle theta with the horizontal.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Block on a frictionless incline"},{"op":"figure","id":"incline","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3,3],"y":[-2,3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"slope","from":[-2.6,-1.501],"to":[2.6,1.501]},{"kind":"segment","from":[-2.6,-1.501],"to":[0,-1.501],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":[-2.6,-1.501],"from":[0,-1.501],"to":[2.6,1.501],"r":0.18,"label":"θ"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[-0.563,-0.325],[0.563,0.325],[0.063,1.191],[-1.063,0.541]],"closed":true},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[-0.25,0.433]}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d8c5cd76-224a-4869-a534-d8e30883c446","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Only two forces act: weight vertically downward, and the normal force perpendicular to the surface. There is no friction force.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"forces","on":"incline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"weight","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[-0.25,-1.567],"arrow":true,"label":"mg"},{"kind":"segment","id":"normalforce","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[-1.116,1.933],"arrow":true,"label":"N"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"normal_eq","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"N=mg\\cos\\theta"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d8c5cd76-224a-4869-a534-d8e30883c446","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Resolve weight along and perpendicular to the slope. These dashed components replace weight in calculations; they are not additional forces.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"components","on":"incline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"parallel","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[-1.116,-0.067],"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"mg sin θ"},{"kind":"segment","id":"perpcomp","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[0.616,-1.067],"arrow":true,"stroke":"dashed","label":"mg cos θ"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"on":"parallel","t":1},"to":{"on":"weight","t":1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"on":"perpcomp","t":1},"to":{"on":"weight","t":1},"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"balance","anchor":{"el":"normal_eq","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\sum F_{\\perp}=N-mg\\cos\\theta=0"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which component of weight accelerates the block down the slope?","expected_gist":"The component parallel to the slope, mg sin θ."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d8c5cd76-224a-4869-a534-d8e30883c446","step":{"id":"s4","script":"The normal force balances the perpendicular component. The remaining downhill force produces acceleration g sine theta, independent of the block's mass.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"motion","on":"incline","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[-1.4,0.4],"to":[-2.353,-0.15],"arrow":true,"label":"a"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"newton","anchor":{"el":"balance","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\sum F_{\\parallel}=mg\\sin\\theta=ma"},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"newton","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\boxed{a=g\\sin\\theta\\quad\\text{down the slope}}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
